<html lang="en">
<head>
    <title>Model Detail Views</title>
    <style>
        h3 { ${REGULAR_LARGE_FONT_STYLE} }
        body { ${REGULAR_FONT_STYLE} }
        code { ${MONOSPACE_FONT_STYLE} }
        h3 code { font-size: inherit; }
        p { margin-top: 0; }
    </style>
</head>
<body style="width: 300px">
    <h3>Model Detail Views</h3>
    <p>When Oracle trains a model, it exposes model-specific information through database views.</p>
    <p>Open them like any other view to inspect details such as model settings, build alerts, or algorithm-specific statistics.</p>
    <p>Common views include:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><code>DM$VG</code> — global model information</li>
        <li><code>DM$VS</code> — computed settings</li>
        <li><code>DM$VW</code> — build alerts</li>
        <li><code>DM$VN</code> — automatic preprocessing</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Algorithm-specific views and their columns vary. A registered view may contain no rows. For example, an empty <code>DM$VW</code> view normally means Oracle recorded no build alerts; it does not mean the view is missing.</p>
</body>
</html>
